{
  "result": "If I could change just one thing, it would be to give everyone the ability to *truly* understand each other.\n\nNot just to hear the words, but to actually feel what the other person is feeling for a moment - their fears, their hopes, their history.\n\nI think so much of the hurt in the world - the arguments, the loneliness, the hate, the wars big and small - comes from misunderstanding. From assuming the worst about each other, or feeling like no one really gets us.\n\nIf we all had that kind of radical empathy built-in, I think kindness would become automatic. People would still disagree, but they'd do it with respect. No one would feel invisible or alone. And we'd be a lot better at solving the *other* big problems together - like hunger, sickness, and inequality.\n\nIt's a quiet superpower, but I think it would change everything.\n\nWhat about you? What would *you* change if you had one wish for the world?",
